# November 20, 2026: southern Lewis County, region mohw (Mohawk Valley west), drawn at random by
# tools/choose.py --state ny, which offered Constableville, Hartwick and Utica. Before this the Atlas had nothing in Lewis
# County: the nearest places were three in Boonville, 12 to 19 km south of Constableville.
# Towns: West Turin (Constableville, Collinsville), Lyonsdale and Lyons Falls, Leyden (Port Leyden, Talcottville),
# Martinsburg (Martinsburg, West Martinsburg) and Watson (Pine Grove). Lowville, the county seat, was left for a session
# working the North Country region.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py), HMdb marker pages, the American Canal
# Society's Black River Canal index (lock by lock, with coordinates), Constable Hall's own pages, the Lyons Falls History
# Association, the 2019 Lyons Falls Brownfield Opportunity Area report (Lewis County), the Village of Lyons Falls and Town of
# Martinsburg pages, the Town of Leyden's history PDF, the Lewis County Historical Society (historicallylewis.org), the
# Pomeroy Foundation's marker pages, NYGenWeb, historypointer.com (Register addresses) and two National Register forms
# (Leyden Common School No. 2, First Lewis County Clerk's Office). The other forms are NPGallery placeholders.
